<sn><md>### Iron ($\text{Fe}$)

* **Role &amp; Function:** 
  - ++Key constituent of blood++ ($50\text{ mg}$ per $100\text{ mL}$ of blood) and 
  - ++primary component++ in `hemoglobin formation`. 
  - ++Stored++ in the `liver, spleen, bones, and red blood cells`.
* +++view
  ![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/dietary_sources_of_iron.png)
  +++  
* **Plant Sources:** Cauliflower, spine amaranths, neem leaf, fig, green banana, maize, wheat, nuts, and millet.
* **Animal Sources:** Fish, meat, eggs, and liver.
* **Deficiency Symptoms:** 
  - Causes ++anemia++, which manifests as `pale eyes`, 
  - `swelling` of hands and legs, 
  - overall `weakness`, `headaches`, and 
  - `heart palpitations`.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Calcium ($\text{Ca}$)

* **Role &amp; Function:** 
  - ++Main constituent++ of `bones and teeth` (making up `~2% of total body weight`, with `90% stored in bones/teeth` alongside phosphorus and magnesium). 
  - Crucial for `blood circulation`, `muscle contractions` (including the heart), and `nerve transmission`.
* +++ view
  ![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/dietary_sources_of_calcium.png)
  +++  
* **Plant Sources:** Pulses, sesame, soybean, cauliflower, carrots, spinach, kochu leaf, red amaranthus, and kalmi leaf.
* **Animal Sources:** Milk, eggs, small fish, and dried fish.
* **Deficiency Symptoms:** Causes 
  - `rickets` in children, 
  - `osteomalacia` in older women, 
  - `delayed tooth` formation in infants, and 
  - impaired `blood circulation`.

</md></sn><sn><md>### Phosphorus ($\text{P}$)

* **Role &amp; Function:** 
  - `Second most abundant` mineral in the body ++after calcium++. 
  - Essential for `bone and tooth` formation, `nucleic acid`/nucleoprotein synthesis, and `energy production` via carbohydrate metabolism. 
  - Stored in `bones, liver, and plasma`.
* +++ view
  ![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-em0n/QDoc/main/BCS/General%20Science/B.Z.Food%20and%20Nutrition/assets/dietary_sources_of_phosphorus.png)
  +++  
* **Plant Sources:** Cereals, beans, peanuts, and tree nuts.
* **Animal Sources:** Eggs, milk, fish, and meat.
* **Deficiency Symptoms:** Causes 
  - `osteoporosis, rickets, and dental` caries (tooth decay). 
  - Deficiencies are rare if adequate protein and calcium are present in the diet.</md></sn>